  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.11.0: ChromaConfigurationOptions.WithChromaCloud says the server is Chroma Cloud behind a proxy or another address. Changes of behavior: a record without metadata keys comes back with an empty Metadata, not null, when the read includes the metadatas; AddAsync, UpdateAsync and UpsertAsync throw an ArgumentException for a metadata without keys and for a list of values of more than one type, as the Python client does; GetAsync throws an ArgumentOutOfRangeException for a negative limit or offset, and returns no record for a limit of 0 without a request; a write that fails after some of its batches went says how many records went, and a collection client made by name does not run it again; deleteRecordsFirst throws a ChromaException and keeps the collection when the server returns records after their delete; ChromaQuery.NResults rejects a negative number. Also: an id condition sends each id once, CreateCollectionAsync and GetOrCreateCollectionAsync reject the names . and .., a connection string takes http and https endpoints only, and the HybridRrf weight of the text never goes below 0. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases. Tested versions: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x",
